@Wangchuk66 | #SonamWangchuk | #NEET | NEET | Sonam Wangchuk | CJP Protest | #CJP https://t.co/xewX56cChv

The government has got the jolt that it required.  The thing to do now is to sit and make processes where the paper leaks stop - not only for NEET, but for every competitive exam - at National and State level. 

Change the "system". The person is inconsequential.  What happens if you change the Minister and #PaperLeak happens again ? 

Whether it is @dpradhanbjp or some other Minister in State Govt. Unless we change the process, leaks will continue to happen. There are far too many corrupt people willing to sell and buy. 

If CJP or any others are actually serious about welfare of youth - the focus should be on process, not just a person. People come and go - if system doesn't change, this whole protest will go waste. 

@NITIAayog should make a blueprint for conduct of exams along with stakeholders. Use technology to close the gaps. It's not so challenging in today's time. After all exams in many countries are being held for years without any leaks. Adopt the best practices.  

@NTA_Exams 
